remstart
    THE SEED OF A GAME
    every game has a seed: a number from 1 to SEED_MAX. two games with the same seed, of the same
    length and mode, start on the same board, are offered the same cards, and get the same quests.
    the player can pick the seed on the page that "New Game" opens, or play the seed of a game on
    the high score tables. otherwise one is picked for them.

    THE STREAMS. `rnd` is no good for this: every bubble and every wobble of a sound takes a number
    from it, and how many of those there are depends on how long the player waited. so the rolls
    that the rules of the game depend on come from three streams of their own, with
    `random stream(RNG_..., max)`, and only those rolls move them on:

        RNG_BOARD   which fish drop in, and the chances of the cards: the stock market, the
                    jellyfish's sting, belly up fish, horror coral, the hidden patterns, the tide
        RNG_CARDS   which cards are offered on the upgrade screen
        RNG_QUESTS  which quest comes next, and what each quest makes up for itself

    they are apart so that the cards and the quests of a seed stay the same however the board is
    played. anything that is only there to be looked at or listened to stays on `rnd`, and so do
    the hints of the hidden game, which are rolled on the clock.

    A NEW ROLL, or a roll that is taken away, or moved, changes what every seed deals from then
    on. GAME_RULES_VERSION has to go up by one whenever that happens, and whenever a rule changes
    what a seed plays like: a new card in the deal, a new quest, a new chance. the test
    seed_deals_the_same_game, in fish_tests_seed, fails when what a seed deals has changed, as a
    reminder.

    ON THE TABLES. a score keeps the seed of its game, the rules version that it was played
    under, and whether the player picked the seed. on this machine those are HISCORE_SEEDS,
    HISCORE_RULES and HISCORE_PICKED. on Steam the seed and the version share the detail
    STEAM_DETAIL_SEED: the seed in the low SEED_BITS bits, and the version in the SEED_RULES_BITS
    above them. STEAM_FLAG_SEED_PICKED says that it was picked. a seed of 0 is a game from before
    there were seeds.
remend

#constant RNG_BOARD 0
#constant RNG_CARDS 1
#constant RNG_QUESTS 2

global SEED_MAX = 250000 `the biggest seed that there is
global SEED_BITS = 18 `how many bits of STEAM_DETAIL_SEED the seed takes
global SEED_RULES_BITS = 14 `and how many the rules version takes, above them
global SEED_RULES_MAX = 16383

` this goes up by one whenever what a seed deals changes. see A NEW ROLL, above.
global GAME_RULES_VERSION = 24 `24: a big group that the cursor pushed a fish into puts it in a bubble, which moves for free until it is in a group, touches another bubble (both pop) or lands on coral (fish_headers_bubbled). 23: ink only moves where the cursor drags it, a swap into ink does nothing to it, and the pot is how many cells have been washed clean, each once, so the ink has to be moved onto new cells (THE INK and CLEAN, fish_headers_squid). 22: the ink left at daybreak stays and spreads by day, a pop washes it, and it pays a pot when it is all gone or is lost at nightfall, a constellation pops as soon as it is made, and coral wipes ink (THE INK OF THE DAY, fish_headers_squid). 21: the coral only spawns at nightfall with a new card, moonlight, which is in the deal (WHEN NIGHT FALLS, THE CORAL SPAWNS, fish_headers_tide). 20: at night, a squid comes to a fish with none of its kind beside it, and three constellations are picked for the sky, both from the board's stream, the sky picking parts of the trident that the game does not have yet, and the squid's jump counted from the fish next to it (fish_headers_squid, fish_headers_neptune). 19: a swap that puts 3 fish together under "think bigger" does not cost the multiplier (THINK BIGGER, fish_headers). 18: the bomb pops the nine fish that it reaches, and "line out" pops the fish of the kind under the cursor in its row or column; neither one copies a fish any more (THE BOMB and LINE OUT, fish_headers). 17: rainbow fish come from a big group, where the cursor was, and a big group bursts them, taking along the pairs beside them (THE BURST, fish_headers_rainbow); they no longer turn up on their own. 16: rainbow fish: a group beside one brings more, and one that pops scores 5 more (THE RAINBOW FISH, fish_headers_rainbow). 15: the starfish (the worm's kind) is never in a school, the same as a crab (fish_routines_school). 14: a quest carries on when the board grows (it used to start over), and the shark only eats what a swap puts together, not what falls after, and a group is the kind that matched, not a fish that the stock market added, and "bunch up" is not a pop (fish_routines_quests). 13: three new cards, flipper, high stakes and tolerance, are in the deal (THREE MORE CARDS, fish_headers_school). 12: a new card, fall in line, is in the deal (fish_headers_school). 11: a school only pops for a match that the carried fish is part of (fish_headers_school). 10: a swap that makes a school grows the school of its kind, in place of popping it (fish_headers_school). 9: at daybreak, every group that the night held and that faces one way is a school (THE DAWN, fish_headers_school). 8: the cursor pops the school of the fish that it carries into a match, and stepping off a fish without one sends its school away; the tide no longer flushes them (fish_headers_school). 7: a swap that the tide wants flushes the schools in the background, which pop and score, and a swap down no longer fills the board from them (fish_headers_school). 6: a school swims off into the background in place of popping, and a swap that goes down fills the board from the schools (fish_headers_school). 5: fish face left or right, and a row of them facing the same way is a school that swims off (fish_headers_school). 4: a shift carries quest marks, a ferry can land on its last pop, and a quest finished as its round ends no longer holds up the next one. 3: 3: the quests were made harder, so that none of them is a round for nothing, and the rounds after the fourth take more and more (HOW LONG A ROUND IS, in fish_headers)

global GAME_SEED = 0 `the seed of the game that is being played. 0 is a game that was saved before there were seeds.
global GAME_SEED_PICKED = 0 `1 when the player picked it
global GAME_SEED_RULES = 0 `the rules version that the game was started under. it is saved with the game.

` the seed that the page that "New Game" opens is set to, or 0 for one that is picked for the
` player. it is 0 every time that the page opens, and it is not remembered.
global OPTION_GAME_SEED = 0

global SAVE_PREF_SEED = 70 `where the seed of the saved game is kept, after SAVE_PREF: the seed, whether it was picked, the rules version, and then two numbers for every stream

` the fish that are waiting above the columns in the quest FORECAST are saved with the game, ten to
` a number, so that a game that is carried on with gets the same fish. see questForeSave.
global QUEST_FORE_PREF = 3700 `forty numbers. it must not move.

` THE SEED ON THE TABLES. three numbers for every row of every table, next to HISCORE_NAMES and
` the others: the seed, the rules version, and whether the seed was picked.
global dim HISCORE_SEEDS(56)
global dim HISCORE_RULES(56)
global dim HISCORE_PICKED(56)
global HISCORE_SEED_PREF = 30 `where a table keeps them in the preferences, after getHighscorePref: three numbers for every row

` on Steam, the seed and the version are the detail STEAM_DETAIL_SEED, and this flag of STEAM_DETAIL_FLAGS
` says that the seed was picked. it is the bit after the four of the modifiers.
global STEAM_FLAG_SEED_PICKED = 128
global STEAM_BIT_SEED_PICKED = 103 `the same flag, as a bit of the whole score: detail 3 starts at bit 96

` THE PAGE WHERE A SEED IS ENTERED. six digits, changed one at a time, the way that the initials
` of a high score are. 000000 is no seed: one is picked for the player.
global dim SEED_DIGITS(6)
global dim SEED_DIGIT_TEXTS(6)
global SEED_DIGIT_GAP = 34 `how far apart the digits are, in pixels

` PLAY THIS SEED. the page of one high score can start a new game on the seed of that score. the
` page sets this to the seed, and the pages under it close, one after the other, and then
` the game starts. see highscore_play_seed in fish_routines_highscores.
global HISCORE_PLAY_SEED = 0
global HISCORE_PLAY_RULES = 0 `the rules version of that score
global HISCORE_PLAY_TABLE = 0 `the table that the score was on, which says the length and the mode of its game

` A NEW GAME ON A SEED, asked for from outside the menu. update_frame, in fish_routines, starts a
` game with the seed, length and mode of the options when this is 1, with no menu and no bubbles.
` the long tests ask, to play one seed twice. see fish_tests_seed.
global REQUEST_SEED_RESTART = 0
